    <statement><p>Two carts, A and B, are connected by a rope <m>39\,ft</m> long that passes over a pulley <m>P</m>. The point <m>Q</m> is on the floor <m>12\,ft</m> directly beneath <m>P</m> and between the carts. Cart A is being pulled away from <m>Q</m> at a speed of <m>2\,ft/s</m>.</p>
<p>How fast is cart B moving toward <m>Q</m> at the instant when cart A is <m>5\,ft</m> from <m>Q</m>?</p>
<p><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/> <m>ft/s</m></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.86710996952412</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
